# There is nothing to copy — this app needs no local setup.
#
# Its configuration is committed and mode-scoped, because none of it is secret:
# a VITE_ variable is inlined into the bundle at build time and is readable by
# anyone who opens the JavaScript. The browser holds no credentials at all —
# every read goes through the API (apps/api), and image/model URLs are public
# bucket links.
#
#   .env.development         `pnpm dev`            → http://localhost:3001
#   .env.production          `pnpm run build:web`  → the Render service
#   .env                     personal overrides — loaded in BOTH modes, so
#                            prefer the two below
#   .env.development.local   personal, dev only     (gitignored)
#   .env.production.local    personal, build only   (gitignored)
#
# Later files win. Vite's own precedence, lowest to highest:
#   .env → .env.local → .env.[mode] → .env.[mode].local
#
# Variables:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL   Origin the browser calls. In dev this is the Vite dev
#                       server itself, which proxies /api to DEV_API_TARGET.
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL   Preconnect hint in index.html. No credentials.
#   DEV_API_TARGET      Dev-proxy target. Read by vite.config.js, not by the
#                       app; no VITE_ prefix, so it never reaches the browser.
#
# Secrets — database URLs, the service-role key, JWT signing — belong to the
# API and live in apps/api/.env.development locally and in the Render dashboard
# in production. Never give one of them a VITE_ prefix.
